The non-certified ServiceNow integration requires enabling global read access to system event and audit tables, which makes those logs accessible to all applications within the instance—not just AppOmni.
This differs from the certified model, which operates within a scoped application boundary and adheres more closely to least privilege principles.
While the non-certified approach enables enhanced threat detection capabilities, it introduces additional security and compliance considerations, particularly in regulated environments, due to the broader access model and reduced isolation.

The non-certified AppOmni integration requires manual deployment and expanded platform-level access to enable full threat detection capabilities.
Key requirements include:
Manual installation of AppOmni via XML update sets and configuration files (not via ServiceNow Store)
Creation of an integration user with OAuth 2.0 authentication, initially configured as a Human identity
Enabling global read access to the sysevent table, making system event logs accessible to all application scopes
Enabling role audit logging (glide.role_management.v2.audit_roles = true) to track permission and role changes
Providing access to audit and event data tables (sys_audit, sys_audit_role) for monitoring and detection
Optional additional table permissions (including write access) if AgentGuard (AI security) is enabled
Configuration of outbound authentication tokens (version dependent)
Recommended database indexing for high-volume tables to maintain performance
Network configuration such as IP allowlisting where required
